92186193730 #edb/ref 1061 52170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193730 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "591346ba-99a7-5721-93c2-821ddfaef9a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193730 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193731 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193731 #edb/ref 1061 52173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193731 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ebbe6b5a-54bb-59dd-88b0-1e010c9ed541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193731 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193732 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193732 #edb/ref 1061 52179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193732 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ac05f5cd-fcfd-545f-8716-67c2baa838d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193732 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193733 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193733 #edb/ref 1061 52183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193733 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b9448a32-13ac-535e-a4d8-7cd491b8a4d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193733 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193734 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193734 #edb/ref 1061 52187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193734 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7036141e-7fee-5677-9ad3-d8da3867d41f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193734 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193735 #edb/ref 1061 52192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193735 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4683a11-1cf6-5a10-a65e-969247f24091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193735 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193914 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following inequality:\n\n$$\n7x -2 < 5x - 18\n$$\n\nAs usual, we solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle. We start by subtracting $5x$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7x - 2 & < 5x - 18 \\\\ 7x - 2 - 5x & < 5x - 18 - 5x \\\\ 2x - 2 & < - 18\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $2$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x - 2 & < - 18 \\\\ 2x - 2 + 2 & < - 18 + 2 \\\\ 2x & < - 16\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x & < - 16 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & < \\frac{-16}{2} \\\\ x & < - 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x < -8$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193914 #edb/ref 1065 8106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193914 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e1c6e185-0d13-5ea0-86f9-e61f64898f5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193914 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193915 #edb/ref 1064 "Now, let's solve an inequality that contains a rational expression:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2y-1}{3} \\lt 5\n$$\n\nFirst, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2y - 1}{3} & < 5 \\\\ 3 \\cdot (\\frac{2y - 1}{3}) & < 3 \\cdot 5 \\\\ 3 \\cdot (\\frac{2y - 1}{3}) & < 15 \\\\ 2y - 1 & < 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2y - 1 & < 15 \\\\ 2y - 1 + 1 & < 15 + 1 \\\\ 2y & < 16 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & < \\frac{16}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & < \\frac{16}{2} \\\\ y & < 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y < 8$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193915 #edb/ref 1065 8107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193915 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "31078899-8e97-5c79-a990-df51f4a9f773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193915 #edb/ref 1067 "Clearing Rational Expressions in Linear Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193916 #edb/ref 1064 "Finally, let's consider an inequality that contains rational expressions on both sides:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x+1}{4} \\leq \\dfrac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we clear the rational expressions by cross-multiplying:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{x + 1}{4} & \\le \\frac{x}{2} \\\\ 2 \\cdot (x + 1) & \\le 4 \\cdot x \\\\ 2x + 2 & \\le 4x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x + 2 & \\le 4x \\\\ 2x + 2 - 2x & \\le 4x - 2x \\\\ 2 & \\le 2x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\le 2x \\\\ \\frac{2}{2} & \\le \\frac{2x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2}{2} & \\le \\frac{2x}{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le x \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\geq 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193916 #edb/ref 1065 8110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193916 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5ec24500-fe0f-5068-b9fa-f19ce733798a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193916 #edb/ref 1067 "Cross-Multiplication in Linear Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
